<article class="env-definition" id="011S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/011S">Definition <span data-tag="011S">12.21.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $(A, E, \alpha , f, g)$ be an exact couple. The <em>spectral sequence associated to the exact couple</em> is the spectral sequence $(E_ r, d_ r)_{r \geq 1}$ with $E_1 = E$, $d_1 = d$, $E_2 = E'$, $d_2 = d' = g' \circ f'$, $E_3 = E''$, $d_3 = d'' = g'' \circ f''$, and so on. </p>
</article>